build: no timestamps in the .apk packages

Every .apk carries a data tar whose entries are stamped with the mtime of the
files on disk. The epoch for mkpkg comes from
scripts/get_source_date_epoch.sh, which reads the package directory's last
commit date with git -- and both the tree and the feeds are cloned --depth 1,
so that git log finds no commit touching most package directories and hands
mkpkg an empty epoch. mkpkg then stamps the build's own clock into every
package, and /lib/apk/db/installed records a different package checksum for
every one of them, so two builds of one commit produced images that differed.

Upstream fixed it by running mkpkg with a fixed epoch (openwrt/openwrt
b0b4bf6e, "build: don't store timestamps in APK packages"). The variable only
reaches mkpkg: the SourceDateEpoch field in the package control still comes
from the package's own source date, and the rootfs timestamps are normalised
to the tree's epoch after install, so nothing on the device changes.

diff --git a/include/package-pack.mk b/include/package-pack.mk
index 9cb64d3..7c2998f 100644
--- a/include/package-pack.mk
+++ b/include/package-pack.mk
@@ -589,7 +589,7 @@
 		exit 1; \
 	fi
 
-	$(FAKEROOT) $(STAGING_DIR_HOST)/bin/apk mkpkg \
+	SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=0 $(FAKEROOT) $(STAGING_DIR_HOST)/bin/apk mkpkg \
 	  --info "name:$(1)$$(ABIV_$(1))" \
 	  --info "version:$(VERSION)" \
 	  $$(if $$(ABIV_$(1)),--info "tags:openwrt:abiversion=$$(ABIV_$(1))") \
